CURATED['/api/compose'] = { post: op('Jobs', `Stitch clips into one video on this computer with ffmpeg (free, $0 in the spend log): JSON {clips: [job id or /files/ URL, …] (1–20, in order; each job's first video output), audio?: job id or /files/ URL (a music bed, trimmed to the video and faded out), voice?: job id or /files/ URL (a narration or dialogue track from 0 s, mixed over the music, which drops to musicVolume, default 0.25 with a voice), musicVolume? (0–2), keepClipAudio? (true: keep each clip's own sound, joined in order, under the music and voice; default false), layout?: "sequence" (default) or "side-by-side" (exactly 2 clips next to each other, e.g. before/after; as long as the shorter one), aspect?: e.g. "9:16", "1:1", "4:5" (centre-crops the result: free cutdowns), title?, fadeOutSec? (0–5, default 1), videoFade? (true: the picture and every sound fade to black over fadeOutSec at the end; default false = only the music fades), trims?: [{in?, out?} | null, …] (seconds, one per clip in clip order, at most one per clip; null or {} = the whole clip; each trim is cut in that clip's own input and clamped to the clip, with a warning when one ran past the end; out must be ≥ 0.1 s after in). Editor fields (all optional): transition "cut" (default) | "crossfade" | "dip" (to black) with transitionSec (0.1–5, default 0.5, capped at 45 % of the shortest clip; each joint shortens the film by it); fit "fit" | "fill" | "blur" with cropX / cropY (0–1, fill's crop point): reframe to aspect from the first clip's short side (240–1080; without fit the older rule below stays); clipVolume / musicVolume / voiceVolume (0–2, gains on tracks first levelled to a set loudness; musicVolume defaults to 0.6 with a voice or clip sound, else 1); duck (default true: music and clip sound dip under the voice, a sidechain compressor) with duckAmount (0–1, default 0.6, about 11 dB); duckClips (default false: the music also dips under the clips' own sound when keepClipAudio; Film turns it on); seams: [{type "cut" | "crossfade" | "fade" (= "dip") | "jcut" | "lcut", sec?} | null, …] (Film: one transition per joint; jcut = a picture cut where the next clip's sound starts sec early, lcut = this clip's sound runs sec past the cut, each shortening the film by sec like a crossfade; seams[i] joins clip i and i+1, null = the film-wide transition; the result lists seams as applied); normalize (default true: every track levelled and the film set to −14 LUFS with a −1.5 dBTP limiter; false = the older raw mix); musicLoop (true: music shorter than the film loops); titleCard / endCard {text, style "clean" | "bold" | "quiet" | "lower", mode "black" (its own segment, adds sec) | "over" (over the first / last clip), sec 1–6 (default 2.5)}; endCard {} uses "Imagination is all you need.". Cards sent as text are drawn on the server; multipart instead of JSON (the JSON in a "body" field) can carry PNG parts titleCard / endCard (the film's size, transparent) and caption strips cue0…cueN with captions: [{start, end, y}] (seconds in the film, y in px).}. Without fit, clips are scaled and padded to the first clip's size at 30 fps (a 9:16 clip in a 16:9 film is pillarboxed, then aspect crops the whole film). Creates a done job (toolId "compose") that shows in Assets. Optional ${AGENT_HDR}. Returns {id, toolId, status, outputs, resultUrl, durationSec, width, height, clips, music, voice, clipAudio, layout, aspect, trims ([{in, out} | null] as applied, null when nothing was cut), videoFade, transition, transitionSec, overlapSec, fit, crop, mix, titleCard, endCard, captions, ducked, loudness {before, target, levels}, warnings, cost: 0, agent}.`,
  { parameters: [AGENT_HP], requestBody: { required: true, content: { 'application/json': { schema: { type: 'object', required: ['clips'], properties: { clips: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, minItems: 1, maxItems: 20 }, audio: { type: 'string' }, voice: { type: 'string' }, title: { type: 'string' }, fadeOutSec: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 5 },
    videoFade: { type: 'boolean' }, keepClipAudio: { type: 'boolean' }, musicVolume: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 2 }, layout: { type: 'string', enum: ['sequence', 'side-by-side'] }, aspect: { type: 'string', pattern: '^\\d{1,2}:\\d{1,2}$' },
    trims: { type: 'array', maxItems: 20, items: { type: ['object', 'null'], properties: { in: { type: 'number', minimum: 0 }, out: { type: 'number', exclusiveMinimum: 0 } } } },
    transition: { type: 'string', enum: ['cut', 'crossfade', 'dip'] }, transitionSec: { type: 'number', minimum: 0.1, maximum: 5 }, fit: { type: 'string', enum: ['fit', 'fill', 'blur'] }, cropX: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 1 }, cropY: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 1 },
    clipVolume: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 2 }, voiceVolume: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 2 }, duck: { type: 'boolean' }, duckAmount: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, maximum: 1 }, normalize: { type: 'boolean' }, musicLoop: { type: 'boolean' },
    titleCard: STITCH_CARD, endCard: STITCH_CARD, captions: { type: 'array', maxItems: 400, items: { type: 'object', properties: { start: { type: 'number' }, end: { type: 'number' }, y: { type: 'number' } } } } } } } } }, responses: { 200: json({ type: 'object' }), 400: err, 500: err } }) };
addParams('/api/tools/{toolId}/price', 'get', [AGENT_HP], 'Agent budgets: with the X-OHF-Agent-Budget header the quote also carries agentBudget {id, name, budgetUsd, spentUsd, remainingUsd, budgetCredits, remainingCredits, thisRunUsd, thisRunCredits, fits}; over budget: runnable false, blockedCode "agent_budget", agentBudgetBlock.');
addParams('/api/models/quote', 'get', [AGENT_HP], 'Agent budgets: agentBudget and (over budget) agentBudgetBlock, exactly as GET /api/tools/{toolId}/price.');
addParams('/api/tools/{toolId}/jobs', 'post', [AGENT_HP], 'Agent budgets: with X-OHF-Agent-Budget, a run over that budget is refused with 400 errorType "limit", code "agent_budget" (remainingUsd, neededUsd…) before the job is created; nothing is sent to a provider. The job and its spend row record the agent (GET /api/jobs/{id} → agent {id, name, budgetUsd, spentUsd}).');
addParams('/api/spend', 'get', [qs('agent', 'Agent budget id, "any" (runs made by any agent) or "none" (your own runs)')], 'Agent budgets: rows carry agentId and agentName (null for your own runs).');
// Step-ETA learning (Oct 21 2026, stepEta.ts): this computer's own timings for local runs
const ETA_RANGE_DOC = 'etaRange (EtaRange: {seconds, low, high, source learned | scaled | reported | first_run, samples, includesLoad cold | warm | null, calibrating, loadSec, secondsPerStep, steps, postSec, key}; also on fit.etaRange). first_run: no number is shown and the run is timed; fit.etaSeconds = etaRange.seconds (null on a first run)';
addParams('/api/tools/{toolId}/price', 'get', [], `Step-ETA: a quote on a local route carries ${ETA_RANGE_DOC}.`);
addParams('/api/tools/{toolId}/price', 'get', [], 'Generate Video (h3-video and its apps, 2026-10-23): perSecond {usd, credits} and perSecondNote ("billed per second of video") only on routes whose price row bills per second (fal, Replicate, MiniMax direct, Comfy Cloud H3, Router Kling / Veo / Seedance / MiniMax H3, LTX, FLUX 3 Video); perSecond × seconds = the run\'s usd within rounding. Flat per-run routes, local (free) routes and token-billed routes with reference video send perSecond null. eta {lowSec, highSec, basis: "measured" | "estimate"} is the same step-ETA range the local quote shows: learned or scaled from this computer\'s runs → measured; a published figure for the GPU class → estimate; null when there is none (hosted routes, first run).');
addParams('/api/models/quote', 'get', [], `Step-ETA: a quote on a local route carries ${ETA_RANGE_DOC}.`);
addParams('/api/jobs/{id}', 'get', [], 'Step-ETA: etaRange (set at submit, refreshed when the local run starts: cold or warm load as things stand then), calibrating (true = the first timed run of this workflow on this computer). While the model loads (no sampler step yet) eta counts down from the learned estimate; after the first step it follows the live step rate.');

// Run on (2026-10-22): no Auto. The pre-selected place, Try on, retry with runOn.
addParams('/api/jobs/{id}/retry', 'post', [qs('runOn', 'Try on <place>: re-run the failed job ONCE on this place (local, comfy-cloud, fal, replicate, bfl…), pinned for this job only, no fallback; your saved choice for the tool + model is not changed. Also accepted as JSON body {runOn}. The reply names route, routing {mode, allowFallback, order}, modelKey, runOn and runOnLabel.'), qs('remember', 'With runOn: true also saves that place as your choice for this tool + model (as Settings › Routing does); reply remembered:true. Default false. Also accepted as JSON body {remember}.')], 'Run on (2026-10-22): body or query runOn re-runs the job on that place (the failed job\'s tryOn lists the ready ones with their price); invalid ids answer 400 invalid_run_on, nothing charged. Every retry (plain, runOn, failedOnly) is checked like a submit (agent budget); it gets its own Spend row (reply estimate). The new job carries rerun: retry | try-on | failed-groups and is not counted as enhanced.');
addParams('/api/tools/{toolId}/jobs', 'post', [], 'Run on (2026-10-22): the reply names the place it will run on: modelKey, runOn, runOnLabel ("Local", "Comfy", "fal"…). Without runOn (or runOn "auto") it runs on the pre-selected place, the same place the quote named; routing.allowFallback is false unless the request sent allowFallback=1. When no place is ready nothing is pre-selected: 402 no_provider (setup, setupOptions), nothing charged.');
addParams('/api/tools', 'get', [], 'Run on (2026-10-22): models[] carry preselect {runOn, label, status, action} | null (the place a model with no saved choice runs on: first ready Comfy → other API (cheapest) → Local, else the mock sample, else null: a place that needs a download, a key or a switch is never pre-selected), autoRunOn (= preselect.runOn, kept for older clients), setup [{runOn, label, action, credits}] (the places that could be set up, same order; Local credits 0 = free per run once set up), rowStatus {kind ready | sample | add_key | download | turn_on | install_node | set_up | coming_soon | unavailable, text, runOn, credits} (one status per picker row) and fromPrice (ready / sample places only; null when nothing runs; an uninstalled GPU is never free); each runsOn row carries group (gpu | comfy | api), detail ("Comfy Cloud" / "Comfy Router" on the Comfy row) and action {kind turn_on | download | install_node | add_key | set_up_gpu, text, missingBytes?, downloadId?} | null; the Local row adds missingBytes when its files don\'t fit on the disk (reasonCode not_enough_disk).');
addParams('/api/tools', 'get', [], 'Model catalogue (2026-10-22, shared/modelRank.ts): every models[] row also carries displayName (name with version, e.g. "Seedance 2.0"), bestFor (one plain line: what the model is good at), rank (per medium, lower = higher; API models before Local models), home ("api" | "gpu"), featured, popular (editorial), aliases (search words), releasedAt (sourced date or null), maker / makerName, caps {summary, …} (image: maxResolution, maxRefs, edit, mask; video: maxResolution, minSeconds, maxSeconds, sound; audio: kind), variantOf and variants (model keys: Z-Image ↔ Z-Image-Turbo). GET /api/models/registry models[] carry the same block as catalogue. Models not on Comfy Router (HY Image 3.5, Muse Image, Fish Audio S2.1 Pro, Sonilo, HeyGen Voice) are Coming soon in every mode.');
addParams('/api/tools', 'get', [], 'Picker sections (2026-10-22, MODEL-PICKER-REVIEW task 5): every models[] row also carries section ("featured": the catalogue featured API models, at most 5 per list, never retiring; "api"; "gpu": best place is your own computer; "soon": nothing can run it here yet) and isNew (releasedAt within 60 days). Rows come sorted by section, then rank, then name; status never reorders them.');
addParams('/api/jobs/{id}', 'get', [], 'Images (transparency, 2026-10-22): feature ({id, name, model, label, workflow} | null): the image feature a job ran as with the real model, e.g. label "Relight · Nano Banana 2" or "Edit Image · GPT Image 2", and the ComfyUI workflow it is credited with ({source: official | community | ours, name, url, author, licence, file?, recipe}). Create Image jobs with a camera rig (cameraBody, lens, focal, aperture) are Camera & Lens and carry input.camera {body, lens, focal, aperture, label, sentence}.');
addParams('/api/tools/{toolId}/price', 'get', [], 'Image Upscale (image-upscale, 2026-10-22): scale=2|4|8 (alias of types=x<n>) is accepted on the quote and on POST /api/tools/image-upscale/jobs. The quote adds scale, workflow (the file that runs for that model and factor), maxSide (8192, lower for some models: Z-Image-Turbo 2K 2048, SeedVR2 3B local 4096) and, with width+height, sourceSize/outputSize (per-megapixel prices bill that output size: fal SeedVR2 / Crystal per MP, Topaz per started 8 or 24 MP). Hosted models (Comfy Router SeedVR2, Crystal, Topaz Wonder 3.5 / Standard V2, fal SeedVR2) have workflow null. A factor the model cannot do → 400 unsupported_scale {allowed}; an output past 8192 px on the long side → 400 output_too_large (the job refuses it too, on every backend). /api/tools tool.app.imageUpscale {maxSide, maxSideByProvider, factors, factorsByProvider, workflows, modelFiles, models (place, label Best detail / Fast / Classic, blurb, price text, measured local seconds, source credit), order}; job.input.workflow and job.feature.workflow name the file that ran.');
